flowchart TD
    PLAN[Immutable projection plan]
    LOCAL[Local Workspace lock]
    WRITE[Lifecycle Write and Verify]
    BRANCH[Branch context]
    PR[Pull request head and base]
    INTEG[Integration ref]
    CHECKS[Required checks and evidence]
    MERGE{Merge eligible?}
    POST[Post-integration refresh]
    CURRENT[Current successor state/status evidence]

    REVAL1{Preflight identities match?}
    REVAL2{Under-lock identities match?}
    REVAL3{Branch identities match?}
    REVAL4{PR head/base/checks match?}
    REVAL5{Integration dependencies current?}

    STALE[Stale or indeterminate]
    BLOCK[Block mutation or integration]
    REGEN[Regenerate from current validation ref]
    ACCEPT[Accepted workflow result]

    PLAN --> REVAL1
    REVAL1 -->|yes| LOCAL
    REVAL1 -->|no| STALE

    LOCAL --> REVAL2
    REVAL2 -->|yes| WRITE
    REVAL2 -->|no| STALE

    WRITE --> BRANCH
    BRANCH --> REVAL3
    REVAL3 -->|yes| PR
    REVAL3 -->|no| STALE

    PR --> REVAL4
    CHECKS --> REVAL4
    REVAL4 -->|yes| INTEG
    REVAL4 -->|no| STALE

    INTEG --> REVAL5
    REVAL5 -->|yes| MERGE
    REVAL5 -->|no| STALE

    MERGE -->|yes| ACCEPT
    MERGE -->|no| BLOCK
    ACCEPT --> POST
    POST -->|accepted ref and dependencies current| CURRENT
    POST -->|stale or unavailable comparison| BLOCK

    STALE --> BLOCK
    BLOCK --> REGEN
    REGEN --> PLAN

    NOTE1[Local lock protects only local Write]
    NOTE2[Workflow serializes branches, PRs and integration]
    NOTE3[Clean textual merge is not freshness proof]
    NOTE4[Historical prose is never auto-merged]
    NOTE5[Evidence explains decisions but is not authority]
    NOTE6[Post-integration refresh runs on the accepted integration ref]

    NOTE1 -. boundary .-> LOCAL
    NOTE2 -. authority .-> BRANCH
    NOTE2 -. authority .-> PR
    NOTE2 -. authority .-> INTEG
    NOTE3 -. warning .-> MERGE
    NOTE4 -. recovery .-> REGEN
    NOTE5 -. evidence .-> CHECKS
    NOTE6 -. refresh .-> POST
